1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,000
PRIOR is a continuity system for recurring DreamDEX Event Contracts.

2
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:25,000
It keeps belief, intent, rules, and evidence connected.

3
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:43,000
A Circuit is a persistent, bounded plan across eligible markets.

4
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:59,000
It carries scope and rules. It does not choose the prediction.

5
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:13,000
A Forecast is one probability committed against one market.

6
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:26,000
The person or agent owns the judgment. The wallet signs it.

7
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:39,000
RFT means Resolution and Forecast Trail.

8
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:58,000
RFT preserves the complete evidence lifecycle for one Forecast.

9
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:09,000
That includes commitment, market, resolution, score, and links.

10
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Workflow: discover, select, verify, set probability, review, sign, read back.

11
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:35,000
When the market changes, stale Forecast and RFT values do not carry over.

12
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Without a wallet provider, PRIOR says provider required.

13
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:54,000
A successful receipt is required before commitment is accepted.

14
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:58,000
Proof shows bounded policy. Economic execution is not claimed.

15
00:02:58,000 --> 00:02:59,400
Forecast captures belief. RFT preserves evidence. Circuit preserves bounded intent.
